# The *default* assumption for the VAULT is that things need to be tracked. The *only* exceptions to that sole assumption are **secrets** and **exhaust**. Tread lightly here.

# ── SECRETS — classes, not specimens, and scoped to the tool dotfolders where they
# live. No global name-shape rules: this vault tracks real files named
# "Precincts_133 (2).csv" and ".claude/settings (2).json" on purpose, so whether a
# salvage-looking name is junk is a human call, never a pattern's. ──
.env
.env.*
*.env
.mcp.json
.*/id_*
.*/*cred*
.*/*token*
.*/auth.json*
.ssh/**

# ── EXHAUST — regenerable byproducts. ──
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ── ANCHORS — always visible. ──
!.gitignore
!/.*/stub.txt
!**.md

# ESTO PERPETUA!
